audit='''# Annotated manifesto pilot: selection and evidence audit\n\n## Selection\n\nStrategy, §§180–206, was selected as the strongest verified cluster in the six reception texts inspected for this pilot. This is a bounded qualitative selection, not a census of the entire dissertation archive. The Power Process and the opening discussion of leftism were alternative candidates; Strategy supplied the clearest concentration of explicit paragraph references across all six checked readers. Section length differs, so raw counts cannot establish normalized reception density.\n\nA keyword triage of 196 attached newspaper pages found zero page-URL hits for “power process” or “surrogate activit…”, four for “leftism/oversocialization”, and 30 for revolution/strategy terms. These are OCR search hits, not verified engagements, and were excluded from annotation counts and the selection claim.\n\nThe strongest initial reading route is §§183, 188, 189, 200, 206. The section is reproduced continuously, including paragraphs with no verified annotation. Absence of a marker means not yet annotated, not no historical reception.\n\n## Base text\n\nThe reading text is the Anarchist Library transcription, whose source note identifies Technological Slavery, not a facsimile of the September 1995 newspaper supplement. Its numbered paragraphs are preserved. Edition differences, OCR/typographic errors, and early printings have not been exhaustively collated. Wikimedia Commons describes the manifesto as author-dedicated public domain: https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Industrial_Society_and_Its_Future.pdf .\n\n## Counting\n\nA response record may cover multiple paragraphs. A paragraph badge counts distinct sources, not repeated quotations or rehostings. The graph shows paragraph/source incidence, not influence, agreement, or organizational membership. Hosted dates are not silently treated as composition dates.\n\n## Paragraph anchors\n\n| Source | Paragraphs | Basis |\n|---|---|---|\n'''
for s in S:
 aa=[a for a in A if a['source']==s['id']];audit+=f"| {s['name']} | {', '.join(map(str,sorted(set(n for a in aa for n in a['paras']))))} | {'; '.join(a['kind'] for a in aa)} |\n"
audit+='\n## Annotation records\n\n'
for a in A:
 s=next(s for s in S if s['id']==a['source']);audit+=f"### {a['id']} — §§{', '.join(map(str,a['paras']))}\n\n{s['name']}, {s['title']}. {s['url']}\n\nRelationship: {a['kind']}. Locator: {a['locator']}.\n\n{a['body']}\n\n"
(out/'selection-audit.md').write_text(audit)
print('27 paragraphs;',len(A),'response records;',len(S),'sources;',sum(bool(p['sources']) for p in P),'annotated paragraphs')
